Figure 5.11 illustrates how the heat transfer model, derived using the electrical analogy, results in an equivalent circuit of thermal resistances arranged in series along the radial direction. The three main resistances modeled in this system are: contact resistance, conduction resistance, and convection resistance.
• The contact resistance is associated with the thermal paste placed between the copper block and the test object. This paste enhances thermal contact,
